ition="float"><label>Fig. 1</label><caption><p>Multiplication of <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic> in cultures supplemented with erythrocytes with various ages, which had been stored <bold>(A)</bold> within EDTA tube and <bold>(B)</bold> within ACD tube. The culture medium was changed every 12 hr.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-1022-g001"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. 2</label><caption><p>Comparison of the parasitemia level of in vitro cultivated <italic>Plasmodium falciparum</italic> in cultures with various intervals of medium change. Results are shown for freshly collected erythrocytes <bold>(A)</bold>, 14-day-old erythrocytes stored in an EDTA tube <bold>(B)</bold>, and 28-day-old erythrocytes stored in an EDTA tube <bold>(C)</bold>.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jkms-22-1022-g002"/></fig></floats-group></article>